  "notes": [
    "Material shader functions and generator code are shared once, independent of building count. Each building references the generator and recipe; no copy of all functions is embedded in each score.",
    "Three.js and OrbitControls are shared vendor code; count once per cold cache, not once per object.",
    "Current viewer lazily fetches read-only source-preview arrays only when source comparison is requested. They are separately accounted, never used by buildGeometry, and not a reconstruction or material runtime dependency.",
    "Original glTF and provenance are retained evidence, not input to reconstruction. They are additional archival bytes outside the categories above.",
    "The common material shader is compiled/cached by Three and varied through uniforms; this is not proof of zero per-instance or per-pixel rendering cost.",
    "Each score retains measured boundary exceptions. The first case has not yet abstracted repeated door/window families; no windows or doors were measured from these source meshes.",
    "Current optional window pattern is a single shared authored receiver controlled by uniforms. It does not claim a complete opening grammar or storey inference.",
    "Future architecture accounting must include shared library once + parameters/composition + preserved exceptions, compared against equivalent information. Individual score-to-source ratios do not measure full-system amortisation.",
    "gzipMemberBytes is the sum of independent deterministic gzip members at level 6, not ZIP size, HTTP transferred size, browser memory or measured performance."
